{
  "name": "Counterparty MTM valuations for audit requests",
  "today": "Counterparties' auditors ask Enron for mark-to-market (MTM) values as of a past date. Confirmations (Joe Hunter, Ellen Wallumrod) has no system that values deals, so for each request they email five or six Risk desk heads. Each desk head forwards it to someone on the desk, who runs a mini-book for that counterparty, exports it to Excel, blacks out the Delta/Vol columns and emails it back. Confirmations then combines the replies.",
  "change": "Give Confirmations a read-only report with back-dated curves that values a counterparty's deals on any desk, so they stop asking the Risk desks.",
  "explanation": "Finish the planned EnTelligence tool, or build an equivalent read-only report, that holds back-dated price curves. Confirmations enters the counterparty's short name and the as-of date. The report returns one combined MTM value and open position across all desks, with no Delta/Vol columns. Confirmations sends that to the auditor. Desk heads and desk staff are no longer involved, and nobody has to forward requests or black out columns by hand.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/240.eml",
      "quote": "Please forward to Ellen Wallumrod the MTM valuation(mini-book) for all \nCoEnergy Trading Company deals as of Dec 31, 2000.  If you can export into \nexcel and forward by e-mail, that would be appreciated."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/214.eml",
      "quote": "Can you provide MTM values as of Dec 29, 2000, for the short name of CROSS \nTIMBERS."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Two more counterparties need MTM values for Dec. 29, 2000."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "We do not have access to \nany system that values these deals, but are looking to get the on-line \n\"EnTelligence\" built so that it carries back-dated curves that will allow us \nto complete these requests without taking up a Risk person's time and without \nhaving to black out information (Delta/Vol) that is included in a mini-book.",
      "note": "Confirmations itself says the planned tool would remove the Risk staff's time and the manual blacking out of columns."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "Until we can get EnTelligence built to our specifications, \nwe'll need to continue to go to the different desks to provide Mark-to-Market \nvaluations for a Counterparty's portfolio.",
      "note": "Every request goes to several desks, so the work is repeated on each desk."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide the total MTM value for that date within your region.",
      "note": "The request goes out again from Risk (Gossett) to five desk heads. Giron forwards it to Carole Frank, who runs the numbers for the West desk."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/136.eml",
      "quote": "The following are the totals for Tudor BVI and Ospraie.  The total MTM value \nfor the West Desk are as follows.  Detail can be found in the attachment.",
      "note": "One desk's share of one request: a desk person computes the totals and attaches the detail. The reply came about an hour after the request reached the desk."
    }
  ],
  "stalls": [],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 3,
    "per": "week",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
    "quote": "we recieve several \nper week"
  },
  "minutes": 45
}

