{
  "name": "Weekly manual compaction of WeaponX Access databases",
  "today": "WeaponX is an Access database that imports and deletes a lot of data every day, and Access does not free the space, so the files grow (one went from 520 MB to 30 MB when compacted). Greg Couch asked every book admin who uses WeaponX, across six managers' groups, to compact their file by hand at least once a week: open it holding the shift key, run Tools/Database Utilities/Compact Database, wait for it to finish, then use it as normal. One admin already does this every day.",
  "change": "Compact every WeaponX file automatically each night so book admins no longer do it by hand.",
  "explanation": "The WeaponX owner or IT sets up one scheduled overnight job per WeaponX file (Access can compact a file from the command line with the /compact switch), or adds a compact step at the end of the daily WeaponX import. Book admins then stop compacting by hand, and every file stays small even when an admin forgets. Setup is a one-time job and is not counted in the savings.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
      "quote": "I would like each of your book admins using WeaponX to begin using the \nfollowing procedures at least once/week (if they aren't already)."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/585.eml",
      "quote": "Try this and see if it does any good."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
      "quote": "Open the database while holding down on the shift key.  This will open the \ndatabase, but prevent the main form from opening automatically.  Next, the \nadmin should go to Access menu selections and choose Tools/Database \nUtilities/Compact Database.",
      "note": "The manual steps each admin repeats: open the file a special way, run compact from the menus, wait for it to finish, and reopen."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
      "quote": "WeaponX imports and deletes \na lot of data on a daily basis.",
      "note": "The files grow every day, so compaction is a standing chore, not a one-off."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
      "quote": "The Texas WeaponX file that I compacted reduced from 520 MB to 30 MB and one \nfor the west went from 400 MB to 12 MB.",
      "note": "Files of hundreds of MB take a while to compact, which is time the admin spends waiting."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
      "quote": "Crystal (East desk I believe) already compacts the database on a daily \nbasis.",
      "note": "At least one admin does it daily, so the weekly figure understates the work."
    }
  ],
  "stalls": [],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 6,
    "per": "week",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/596.eml",
    "quote": "I would like each of your book admins using WeaponX to begin using the \nfollowing procedures at least once/week"
  },
  "minutes": 10
}

