{
  "name": "Monthly P&L top pages for Arthur Andersen's gas testing",
  "today": "Each month the auditors from Arthur Andersen (Mark Austin, Sharon Smith, Carrie Richardson) email the gas Risk desk heads (Kelly, Keiser, Giron, Baumbach) a list of books. For each book they want the P&L top page for the last day of the month. If most of the P&L comes from curve shift, they also want the top pages and curve shift reports for the five largest days. Each desk head forwards the email to two to seven book admins. The admins pull the reports from ERMS and print or copy them, and the desk head passes them on to the auditors. The auditors chase missing books ('2nd request', quarter-file close-out) and ask who is responsible for each desk.",
  "change": "Save every book's month-end and daily P&L top pages and curve shift reports to a read-only audit folder at month-end, so the auditors stop sending requests to the desks.",
  "explanation": "At month-end close, a scheduled ERMS job (or a macro a book admin runs once) saves each gas book's month-end top page, its daily top pages and its Gas Daily curve shift reports as PDF files. They go into a read-only folder, one subfolder per month, with a one-page index that lists each book and the book admin responsible for it. ERMS can already show most reports as Adobe Acrobat files. The auditors get read access, or a copy of the folder if they no longer have Enron network access. They choose their books and the five largest days from the folder themselves. Desk heads and book admins no longer forward, pull, print or copy reports, and nobody has to chase missing books. Calls to discuss the P&L drivers stay as they are, and so do requests for deal tickets and confirmations.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/583.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide the top sheets relating to the following desk:  West Firm, \nNorth West Firm, Central Firm, Texas Intra-Month, and Central Intra-Month."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/516.eml",
      "quote": "In order for us to complete our monthly gas testing, please provide the \nfollowing items."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/515.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide us with the P&L top sheet as of October 31 for the following \nbooks."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/420.eml",
      "quote": "In review of our third quarter file, we have not received the P&L top pages \nor curve shift reports for the following regions:  West Firm, FT Northwest \nand Mgmt. West."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/317.eml",
      "quote": "We are requesting that you supply the P & L top pages for the \nlast day of the month for those regions that are applicable to you."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/201.eml",
      "quote": "Please make sure this guy gets what he needs."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/516.eml",
      "quote": "Additionally, if the majority of \nthe P&L pertains to curve shift, please provide the P&L top pages for five \nof  the largest days including the Curve Shift Reports.",
      "note": "For each book, the admin may have to pull six top pages plus curve shift reports, not just one page. One request listed seven books."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/516.eml",
      "quote": "Please get this info to me and I will pass it on to AA.",
      "note": "Giron sends the request on to four staff, then collects their reports and passes them to the auditors."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/201.eml",
      "quote": "To: William Kelly/HOU/ECT@ECT, Kam Keiser/HOU/ECT@ECT, Darron C \nGiron/HOU/ECT@ECT, David Baumbach/HOU/ECT@ECT, Jody Crook/Corp/Enron@ENRON, \nPhillip M Love/HOU/ECT@ECT, Jason Wolfe/NA/Enron@ENRON, Chris \nWalker/HOU/ECT@ECT, Carole Frank/NA/Enron@ENRON, Jennifer \nBagwell/NA/Enron@ENRON, O'Neal D Winfree/HOU/ECT@ECT",
      "note": "Each monthly request involves four desk heads and several book admins. Giron alone then forwards it to seven people."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/420.eml",
      "quote": "Pull this together and then call Sharon so they can come get the copies.",
      "note": "The reports are handed over as paper copies, which the auditors have to come and collect."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/299.eml",
      "quote": "please direct me to the individual responsible \nfor each of the desks listed below.",
      "note": "The auditors do not know who handles each book. The index of book admins would answer this."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/inbox/190.eml",
      "quote": "Most reports can be viewed on the screen using Adobe Acrobat.",
      "note": "ERMS can already produce the reports as files, so saving them to a folder needs little new work."
    }
  ],
  "stalls": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/317.eml",
      "quote": "Is there someone else that can direct us to?  I would like to get this \ninformation as soon as it is possible.",
      "note": "The auditors' testing waits while the desk head is travelling, because only he routes the request."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/420.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide this information as we would like to close \nout our third quarter file.",
      "note": "The auditors cannot close their quarterly file until the missing reports arrive."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 1,
    "per": "month",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/317.eml",
    "quote": "As part of our monthly testing"
  },
  "minutes": 180
}

